<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Reopen from grid → rehydrate session + review state + files</title>
    <phase>3 Hub</phase>
    <gate>deps 030,020,025 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Frontend (.tsx) session-rehydration flow crossing the session-binding + persistence spine; user-facing three-pane reopen; FULL per §8 (frontend + session-state judgment).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Wiring reopen against already-built binding (020) + persistence (025) seams; specified integration, not architectural design — sonnet default.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Depends on the hub widget (030) plus the binding (020) + persistence (025) seams; touches shared three-pane reopen path — serialize after 030 within W4.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030,020,025</deps>
    <tags>frontend, spaarkeai, session</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Wire the hub grid's row-open action: selecting a sprk_analysis row opens the three-pane SpaarkeAi surface with that
    analysis fully rehydrated — its session transcript (from Cosmos via the session↔Analysis binding), its findings /
    review state, and its files (resolved via the sprk_documentid → sprk_document SPE hop). Reopening restores prior
    state; it MUST NOT silently create an empty session.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the SpaarkeAi three-pane surface, the session↔Analysis binding + Cosmos
    persistence tiers, and the sprk_document SPE file-resolution hop. Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Selecting a grid row opens the three-pane surface for that Analysis with (a) its session history restored from the
    durable transcript via the binding, (b) findings/review state restored, and (c) its files loaded via the
    sprk_documentid hop; a TTL-expired or stale session resolves against Cosmos rather than creating an empty one.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-11: reopen from the grid rehydrates session + review state + files. The binding (task 020) associates a
      session to a sprk_analysis; Cosmos is the transcript store-of-record (ADR-040 Path A — Dataverse holds the anchor
      + outputs). Persistence hardening (task 025) makes stale/expired server sessions resolve against Cosmos instead
      of minting an empty session, anchors tab persistence on the Analysis record, and restores editor edit-state.
      Files are NOT duplicated on sprk_analysis — they resolve through sprk_documentid → sprk_document (SPE hop,
      ADR-007). This task consumes those seams; it does not rebuild them.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/AnalysisHubWidget.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/events/PaneEventTypes.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/registry/WorkspaceWidgetRegistry.ts</file>
      <file role="dependency">the session↔Analysis binding + reopen seam delivered by task 020</file>
      <file role="dependency">the Cosmos-resolve + tab-anchor + edit-restore behavior delivered by task 025</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">Hub widget + grid — the row whose selection triggers reopen.</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">Session↔Analysis FK binding — how the Analysis maps to its durable session/transcript.</dependency>
      <dependency task="025" status="pending">Persistence hardening — stale→Cosmos resolve, tab anchor on Analysis, edit restore.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">SCOPE: transcript rehydration. Restore session history from the Cosmos transcript store-of-record via the binding; Dataverse holds the anchor + outputs only (Path A). Do NOT read the retired sprk_chathistory legacy path for rehydration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">SCOPE: file restore. Resolve the Analysis's files via sprk_documentid → sprk_document SPE hop; MUST NOT read duplicated SPE pointers off sprk_analysis.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: reopen behavior. A TTL-expired/stale session MUST resolve against Cosmos (task 025), never silently create an empty session (no history loss). Tab open is anchored on the Analysis record, not gated on chatSessionId.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">SCOPE: mount signalling. Open the three-pane surface via the PaneEventBus widget_load event (per PaneEventTypes.ts), consistent with the surface-launch mechanism — do NOT invent a bespoke open path.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spe-file-store.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-030-pane-event-bus.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKEAI-WORKSPACE-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/ASSISTANT-SURFACE-LAUNCH-MECHANISM.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="widget_load mount event" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/events/PaneEventTypes.ts">
        Emit the PaneEventBus widget_load event to mount/open the three-pane surface for the selected Analysis.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Session↔Analysis binding" location="task 020 binding seam">
        Map the selected sprk_analysis to its durable session via the FK binding; resolve the transcript from Cosmos.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare RIGOR LEVEL: FULL. Confirm the shape of the 020 binding seam and the 025 Cosmos-resolve/edit-restore behavior before wiring.</step>
    <step order="1">Add the grid row-open handler in AnalysisHubWidget: on row selection, resolve the Analysis id + its bound session.</step>
    <step order="2">Open the three-pane surface (PaneEventBus widget_load) for the Analysis, anchoring the tab on the Analysis record (not chatSessionId).</step>
    <step order="3">Rehydrate the session transcript from Cosmos via the binding; if the server session is stale/expired, resolve against Cosmos rather than minting an empty session.</step>
    <step order="4">Restore findings/review state for the Analysis.</step>
    <step order="5">Resolve and load the Analysis's files via sprk_documentid → sprk_document SPE hop.</step>
    <step order="6">Add ui-tests (reopen restores history + review + files; stale session does not lose history; ADR-021 dark-mode) and run them.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 031 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If rehydration would cross the RETIRED legacy session path (AnalysisEndpoints /continue|/resume, sprk_chathistory read) — because the binding/Cosmos seam does not yet cover a case — STOP, note it, and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than reviving the legacy path (retirement is tasks 062/064).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Reopen restores full state">
      <steps><step>Select a grid row for an Analysis with prior history, findings, and files.</step></steps>
      <expected>The three-pane surface opens showing the restored session transcript, findings/review state, and the Analysis's files.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Stale session does not lose history">
      <steps><step>Reopen an Analysis whose server session has passed TTL.</step></steps>
      <expected>Prior history is restored from Cosmos; NO empty session is silently created.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Tab anchored on Analysis">
      <steps><step>Reopen an Analysis, then refresh.</step></steps>
      <expected>The tab persists anchored on the Analysis record, not gated on chatSessionId.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark-mode">
      <steps><step>Reopen an Analysis under the dark Fluent theme.</step></steps>
      <expected>The reopened three-pane surface renders with correct contrast using Fluent v9 tokens.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the shared lib + widget (build:prod for production output).</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/AnalysisHubWidget.tsx (row-open + rehydrate wiring)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/__tests__/AnalysisHubWidget.reopen.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a grid row for an existing Analysis, when it is selected, then the three-pane surface opens with that analysis's session history, findings/review state, and files restored (FR-11 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a TTL-expired server session, when the Analysis is reopened, then prior history is restored from Cosmos and no empty session is created.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a reopened Analysis, when the page refreshes, then the tab persists anchored on the Analysis record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Files restore via sprk_documentid → sprk_document SPE hop; no SPE pointers are read off sprk_analysis.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: rehydration never reads the retired sprk_chathistory / AnalysisEndpoints legacy path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADR-021: reopened surface renders correctly in both light and dark themes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit/ui tests pass; shared-lib build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec FR-11 (§126-128). Consumes the 020 binding + 025 persistence seams — do not rebuild them. Reuse the
    PaneEventBus widget_load mount path (ASSISTANT-SURFACE-LAUNCH-MECHANISM.md). Findings/review widgets
    (FindingsWidget / NdaReviewSummaryPanel) survive retirement and are reused for review-state restore.

    COMPLETED (2026-07-29). Implementation summary + deviations:

    - New thin BFF endpoint GET /api/ai/chat/sessions/by-analysis/{analysisId} (ChatEndpoints.cs) resolves
      the Analysis's bound session via the task-020 GetSessionsByAnalysisAsync FK query (no such lookup
      was previously exposed to clients). Picks the MOST RECENTLY CREATED session (archived or not — an
      archived session still holds its transcript per task 022). Selection logic extracted to an
      `internal static SelectMostRecentSession` helper, unit-tested directly (4 tests) — see
      tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/Ai/ChatEndpointsSessionByAnalysisTests.cs. DEVIATION: no
      HTTP-level contract test for the route itself — building a MapChatEndpoints()-hosting fixture would
      require wiring that group's very large DI graph (RAG, SprkChatAgentFactory, session persistence,
      etc.); no such fixture exists anywhere in the suite today. Accepted as a Path A (project-scoped)
      exception per code-review — flagged as optional follow-up if full route coverage is wanted.

    - AnalysisHubWidget.tsx reopens IN PLACE (no page reload) since the widget is itself already a tab
      inside the open three-pane it is rehydrating. Row-open wires through DataverseEntityViewWidget's
      existing (but previously unused) `onRecordOpen` DataGrid escape hatch — added as an optional
      pass-through prop on DataverseEntityViewWidgetData (small, additive extension, not a fork).
      Dispatches (a) a NEW additive `conversation.session_switch` PaneEventBus discriminant (reuses the
      existing `sessionId` field on ConversationPaneEvent — see PaneEventTypes.ts) that ConversationPane
      routes to its EXISTING `handleSelectHistorySession` (the History-menu session-select handler) — this
      is TTL-safe because ChatSessionManager.GetSessionAsync (task-025 hardening) already falls back
      Redis→Cosmos→Dataverse; and (b) for a linked file, a `workspace.widget_load` document-viewer event
      with a live fetchPreviewUrl closure (ADR-007 hop, restated locally per the ADR-012 boundary — shared
      lib cannot import the solution-owned analysisFileResolution.ts). Setting chatSessionId ALSO drives
      WorkspacePane's existing chatSessionId-keyed /tabs restore effect, covering review/findings-state
      restore for free (no new code needed there).
      DEVIATION from the POML's literal file-scope: this required a small additive change to
      ConversationPane.tsx (one usePaneEvent subscription reusing the existing handler) and PaneEventTypes.ts
      (one new union member) — investigated and rejected alternatives: (1) a full-page reload via
      ?sessionId= URL param — zero touches to ConversationPane but heavier UX and not what "reuse the
      existing three-pane open path" was found to mean once traced; (2) persisting a document-viewer tab
      via the /tabs PATCH endpoint before navigating — rejected because DocumentViewerWidget's
      fetchPreviewUrl closure cannot survive JSON serialization (a persisted static previewUrl would be
      stale by restore time). The in-place approach was the only one that genuinely satisfies "TTL-expired
      resolves against Cosmos, never mints an empty session" (acceptance criterion 2) without duplicating
      task-025's restore logic.

    Build/test: dotnet build Sprk.Bff.Api (0 errors) + 4 new BFF unit tests pass; Spaarke.AI.Widgets
    `npm run build` (tsc, 0 errors) + full jest suite (680/681 pass — the 1 pre-existing failure in
    register-workspace-widgets.test.ts, "Communications" vs "Messages" metadata, is unrelated to this task
    and predates it); SpaarkeAi `npm run typecheck` (0 surface-owned errors) + ConversationPane/WorkspacePane
    jest suites (223/223 pass).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files. Follow task-execute incl. Step 9.5 gates (FULL: code-review + adr-check).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
